# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out native on Windows,
# which is what core.autocrlf=true was already doing implicitly for everyone here. Written down so
# it does not depend on a machine-local git setting: a contributor with autocrlf=false would
# otherwise commit CRLF and produce a diff touching every line of a file nobody edited.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts - a .sh with CRLF fails at the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine either way and is authored here with a UTF-8 BOM; leave it native.
*.ps1 text

# Binary, so git never tries to translate them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
